Good question 🔥
This is the **core concept** you must master for cinematic GSAP architecture.

You have multiple sections:

* Hero Video
* Logo Reveal
* Menu Frame
* (Later Swan, Bubble, etc.)

And you want strict order control.

---

# 🎯 The Correct Way To Control Order

There are only **3 reliable ways** to control GSAP timeline order:

---

# ✅ METHOD 1 (BEST) → Use `">"` chaining

This is the cleanest and most professional way.

It means:

> “Start this after the previous animation ends.”

---

## 🔥 Example – Your Exact Case

### 🧩 In your parent (where masterTl is created)

```ts
const masterTl = useRef(
  gsap.timeline({ paused: false })
);
```

---

### 1️⃣ Hero

```ts
masterTl.current.add(heroTl);
```

---

### 2️⃣ Logo Reveal

```ts
masterTl.current.add(logoTl, ">");
```

---

### 3️⃣ Menu Frame

```ts
masterTl.current.add(menuTl, ">");
```

---

### What `">"` means

It literally means:

```
Place this at the END of the previous animation.
```

So order becomes:

```
Hero
  ↓
Logo
  ↓
Menu
```

No labels needed.
No guessing.
No race conditions.

---

# ✅ METHOD 2 → Use Labels (When You Need Control)

Use labels only if:

* You need delays
* You need branching
* You need mid-timeline inserts

Example:

```ts
masterTl.add(heroTl);
masterTl.addLabel("after-hero", ">");
masterTl.add(logoTl, "after-hero");
masterTl.add(menuTl, "logo-end+=1");
```

⚠️ But labels are error-prone if placed incorrectly (like your earlier issue).

---

# ✅ METHOD 3 → Absolute Time (Not Recommended for You)

```ts
masterTl.add(heroTl, 0);
masterTl.add(logoTl, 8);
masterTl.add(menuTl, 12);
```

Only good for fixed duration projects.
Not flexible.

---

# 🧠 Why Your Sequence Was Breaking

Because:

```ts
masterTl.current.addLabel("after-hero");
```

Without specifying position defaults to time 0.

So Logo started at time 0 instead of after Hero.

---

# 🏗 BEST STRUCTURE FOR YOUR PROJECT

Since you're building a cinematic landing page:

Create timelines inside each component
But **only add them sequentially using `">"`**

---

## 🧩 HERO COMPONENT

```ts
masterTl.current.add(heroTl);
```

---

## 🧩 LOGO COMPONENT

```ts
masterTl.current.add(logoTl, ">");
```

---

## 🧩 MENU COMPONENT

```ts
masterTl.current.add(menuTl, ">");
```

---

# 💡 Important Rule

Never mix:

* Labels
* Absolute times
* and `">"`

In the same sequence unless you really understand timing.

For your use case → stick to `">"`.

---

# 🎬 Final Visual Timeline

```
Master Timeline
    ├── Hero (full video duration)
    ├── Logo Reveal
    └── Menu Frame
```

Guaranteed order.
Clean architecture.
No overlap bugs.

